WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:18.579
know why someone would take the movie tickets but not these games," Cole said.

2
00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:19.980
"It's simple.

3
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.561
The thief stumbled across that plastic container.

4
00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:24.682
But he didn't find this treasure chest."

5
00:00:24.702 --> 00:00:27.323
"Yeah," Luke agreed.

6
00:00:27.343 --> 00:00:30.104
"William's parents said that's probably what happened."

7
00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:34.925
"I still think Roger Redbeard stole our tickets," Maggie added.

8
00:00:34.945 --> 00:00:38.266
"He probably didn't notice the clue in the box."

9
00:00:38.286 --> 00:00:42.908
"It's a good thing he didn't know about this booty," Nathan said.

10
00:00:42.928 --> 00:00:46.949
"We wouldn't have our awesome new game players right now!"

11
00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.350
Henry didn't say anything.

12
00:00:50.071 --> 00:00:52.091
He still wasn't sure that Roger was the thief.

13
00:00:52.731 --> 00:00:53.952
They needed more evidence.

14
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.462
Henry was still thinking as they started to walk back to the beach.

15
00:01:04.302 --> 00:01:06.743
He had to find out if Roger had really walked to town.

16
00:01:06.763 --> 00:01:09.165
"Hey, Anna," he said.

17
00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:13.607
"Did you see Roger walking by the surf while we were all checking the tide pools?"

18
00:01:14.628 --> 00:01:15.208
Anna blinked.

19
00:01:15.228 --> 00:01:16.388
"Excuse me?"

20
00:01:16.829 --> 00:01:17.289
she said.

21
00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:19.870
Henry repeated his question.

22
00:01:20.831 --> 00:01:21.631
She shook her head.

23
00:01:21.651 --> 00:01:24.873
"I didn't go down by the surf," she replied.

24
00:01:24.893 --> 00:01:27.815
"My tide pool wasn't close to the water."

25
00:01:27.835 --> 00:01:30.216
"Really?" Maggie said.

26
00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.530
"Because Roger said he saw you running through the surf."

27
00:01:34.891 --> 00:01:35.311
"He did?"

28
00:01:35.751 --> 00:01:36.272
Anna said.

29
00:01:37.272 --> 00:01:38.533
Then she gave a quick smile.

30
00:01:38.553 --> 00:01:40.595
"Oh, I know.

31
00:01:41.095 --> 00:01:42.336
I bet he saw my sister.

32
00:01:43.156 --> 00:01:44.797
She's only two years older than I am.

33
00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.179
A lot of people think we look alike.

34
00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.401
She was probably jogging.

35
00:01:50.141 --> 00:01:51.742
She loves to exercise."

36
00:01:52.723 --> 00:01:54.544
Henry thought of another question for Anna.

37
00:01:54.564 --> 00:01:57.626
"How long does it take to walk to town from here?"

38
00:01:57.646 --> 00:02:01.296
"About fifteen or twenty minutes," Anna replied.

39
00:02:02.477 --> 00:02:04.898
Cole wasn't paying much attention to the conversation.

40
00:02:05.559 --> 00:02:07.100
He was staring at the next clue.

41
00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.562
"It's a drawing of some buildings," he said.

42
00:02:10.582 --> 00:02:12.463
"Close to a park or something."

43
00:02:13.463 --> 00:02:15.524
"I think we have to go into town," said Luke.

44
00:02:15.544 --> 00:02:17.705
"We can play our games on the way."

45
00:02:20.207 --> 00:02:22.508
Everyone started walking up the beach toward town.

46
00:02:23.589 --> 00:02:25.990
When they passed William's house, William stopped.

47
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.472
"I'll catch up with you in a few minutes," he said.

48
00:02:30.592 --> 00:02:32.373
"These sandals are giving me blisters.

49
00:02:33.613 --> 00:02:35.154
I want to put on different ones."

50
00:02:37.455 --> 00:02:41.036
Without waiting for an answer, he ran ahead and disappeared into his house.

51
00:02:42.477 --> 00:02:43.817
The others stared after him.

52
00:02:43.837 --> 00:02:46.499
"What's wrong with William today?"

53
00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:48.059
Nathan said with a frown.

54
00:02:48.079 --> 00:02:50.380
"He seems grouchy.

55
00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.381
It's almost like he wishes we weren't here."

56
00:02:54.482 --> 00:02:56.242
Henry had been thinking the same thing.

57
00:02:56.983 --> 00:02:57.803
He just shrugged.

58
00:02:57.823 --> 00:02:59.044
"I'm not sure."

59
00:03:01.516 --> 00:03:02.717
They all kept walking.

60
00:03:03.378 --> 00:03:06.320
Everyone except Henry was focused on their video game players.

61
00:03:07.481 --> 00:03:11.465
Soon Henry poked Cole and Maggie, gesturing for them to slow down.

62
00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:17.890
He wanted The Lemonade Detectives to whisper to one another without anyone else overhearing.

63
00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.112
"What do you guys think?"

64
00:03:20.632 --> 00:03:21.913
Henry asked quietly.

65
00:03:21.933 --> 00:03:27.818
"If Roger really walked to town and back, it took him at least half an hour."

66
00:03:27.838 --> 00:03:33.756
"Plus however long it took him to go into a store and buy that soda," Cole pointed out.

67
00:03:33.776 --> 00:03:38.660
"That means he didn't have time to steal our tickets," Maggie added.

68
00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.783
"If he's telling the truth, that is."

69
00:03:42.904 --> 00:03:43.644
Cole nodded.

70
00:03:43.664 --> 00:03:45.826
"We still don't know for sure.

71
00:03:46.527 --> 00:03:48.048
Anna said she didn't see him, remember?"

72
00:03:48.068 --> 00:03:49.570
"I know."

73
00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:54.494
Henry glanced forward to make sure the others weren't listening.

74
00:03:54.514 --> 00:04:00.178
"When we get to town, let's try to find out if he really bought that soda there."

75
00:04:00.198 --> 00:04:02.240
"How are we going to do that?"

76
00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:03.341
Cole asked.

77
00:04:03.361 --> 00:04:07.023
"There was a logo on the cup," Henry replied.

78
00:04:07.043 --> 00:04:09.405
"It said SCGS.

79
00:04:10.606 --> 00:04:12.748
Maybe we can find a business with that name."

80
00:04:13.848 --> 00:04:15.189
"Okay," Cole said.

81
00:04:15.209 --> 00:04:17.191
"But what about our other suspects?"

82
00:04:17.211 --> 00:04:20.833
"Like William, for instance," Maggie said.

83
00:04:20.853 --> 00:04:24.156
"It's pretty suspicious that he ran off by himself."

84
00:04:25.036 --> 00:04:27.738
"This is the second time he's done that," Cole said.

85
00:04:27.758 --> 00:04:31.340
"He left when he and I were supposed to be searching together too."

86
00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:35.043
"That is suspcious," Henry agreed.

87
00:04:35.063 --> 00:04:37.365
"We should pay attention to William.

88
00:04:37.845 --> 00:04:39.746
And to Anna, Luke, and Nathan."

89
00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.989
"I still don't think Nathan would steal anything," Cole said.

90
00:04:44.009 --> 00:04:49.733
"I know he's acting kind of grouchy today, but—" Cole stopped short.

91
00:04:50.614 --> 00:04:51.514
Henry saw why.

92
00:04:52.275 --> 00:04:53.856
Luke was dropping back to join them.

93
00:04:54.984 --> 00:04:57.306
"Keep up, you guys," he said with a smile.

94
00:04:57.326 --> 00:05:00.908
"Otherwise we might not share the next pirate booty with you!"

95
00:05:01.869 --> 00:05:02.690
Henry chuckled.

96
00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.392
Since Luke was there, he decided to try to question him.

97
00:05:06.412 --> 00:05:09.975
"It's too bad about those missing movie tickets, huh?"

98
00:05:10.275 --> 00:05:10.715
he said.

99
00:05:10.735 --> 00:05:15.779
"You're such a big fan of pirates, I bet you'd love to go to that premiere."

100
00:05:16.759 --> 00:05:17.700
Luke didn't answer.

101
00:05:18.481 --> 00:05:19.621
Henry looked over at him.

102
00:05:20.542 --> 00:05:22.964
To Henry's surprise, Luke wasn't smiling anymore.

103
00:05:23.604 --> 00:05:25.486
His face was turning bright red.

104
00:05:25.506 --> 00:05:29.771
"Um, actually, about those movie tickets Luke muttered.

105
00:05:30.691 --> 00:05:31.913
Henry's eyes widened.

106
00:05:32.553 --> 00:05:34.515
Was Luke about to confess to the crime?
